From 970944cee9c2276e6533e1d10eb1ac47a3d7b07f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode): price MMA tile knees, 64-row wave
 saturation, and context bands in _step_cost

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.

Rationale:
On NVIDIA GB10 (48 SMs, sm_121a), AdaptiveVerificationManager._step_cost() previously applied HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.55 to all verification rows above HIGH_ROW_COST_KNEE = 16 with no upper bound and ignored request context length except when global KV pool occupancy exceeded 70%:
1. Across 40-layer Dense FP8 projections, SparseMlaV41Plan, and 8-layer IndexerV41Plan on GB10, crossing R = 16 -> 17 rows jumps from the 1-tile decode_16 kernel into the 2-tile decode_32 kernel (+1,200.3 us / +79.6% dense GEMM latency).
2. Above R = 64 rows on 48 SMs, dense projections cross DECODE_ROWS = 64 into prefill_128 (+2,692.2 us / +95.7% at R = 80), _index_chunk crosses DECODE_CHUNK = 64 into a second 64-row wave, and routed MoE expert union (64 * 6 = 384 slots across 256 experts) saturates. Leaving HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.55 unbounded above 64 rows caused c16/c32 cohorts to drop the first-draft survival threshold to ~0.33 and spill into the 80..96-row second wave.
3. At long context lengths (16K..128K tokens) where global KV page occupancy remains below 70%, per-row IndexerV41Plan + SparseMlaV41Plan cost rises from 0.4 us/row at 2K to 21.1 us/row at 16K (4-layer ratio=1 reindex saturation at L = 16,384) and 95.7..102.8 us/row at 128K (3-layer ratio=2 full-index scan), and does not coalesce in the 17..64-row regime.

Calibrate _step_cost(), effective_dead_rows_tau(), and get_num_tokens() using deterministic, rank-invariant tensor metadata:
- Add three-regime MMA-tile and wave-saturation pricing (HIGH_ROW_COST_KNEE = 16 at 0.55x, SATURATED_ROW_COST_KNEE = 64 returning to SATURATED_ROW_COST_SCALE = 1.0x, MMA_TILE_STEP_ROWS = 0.25 per 16-row boundary up to 64 rows, SINGLE_REQ_TILE_STEP_ROWS = 1.5 at the c=1 16 -> 17 row boundary, and SECOND_WAVE_STEP_ROWS = 2.0 above 64 rows).
- Add two-slope context-length row-cost scaling _context_row_cost_scale() (CONTEXT_ROW_COST_KNEE = 8192, CONTEXT_REINDEX_SATURATION = 16384 with weight 0.12, CONTEXT_SOURCE_SPAN = 65536 with slope 0.22, capped at CONTEXT_MAX_ROW_COST_SCALE = 2.25), applied as uncoalesced per-row excess cost in _step_cost(), scaled into effective_dead_rows_tau(), and used to prioritize short-context draft slots during get_num_tokens() reallocation.

Quality:
Preserves exact target rejection-sampling verification semantics and rank-invariant token budgets across TP ranks while curbing low-yield draft admission across the 16-row single-request MMA boundary, the 64-row second-wave saturation knee, and 16K..128K long-context regimes.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py across 2 fresh container boots (44 passed, 1 skipped).

Upstream status: local GB10 SM121 adaptive verification cost model calibration.
