-# Two-slope verification row-cost knee: once a step crosses one 16-row Tensor
-# Core MMA tile, additional verification rows share the already-launched expert
-# and dense weight tiles at a reduced marginal cost.
+# Three-regime verification row-cost curve on SM120 / SM121:
+# 1) rows <= 16: single 16-row Tensor Core MMA tile (block_M=16) and early
+#    MoE PDL trigger (slope 1.0x).
+# 2) 17 <= rows <= 64: multi-request rows pack into decode_32 / decode_64 MMA
+#    tiles and share active MoE expert tiles at a 0.55x marginal slope, with
+#    discrete tile-step costs at the 16->17 and 32->33 MMA boundaries. A
+#    single request spilling past 16 rows has no cross-request expert
+#    coalescing and pays the full 1.0x slope plus the second-tile jump.
+# 3) rows > 64: dense projections exceed DECODE_ROWS=64 into prefill_128 /
+#    multi-tile waves, attention indexers split into a second 64-row
+#    DECODE_CHUNK, and MoE experts saturate, returning the marginal slope to
+#    1.0x plus a discrete wave-boundary step per 64-row chunk.
 HIGH_ROW_COST_KNEE = 16
 HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.55
+SATURATED_ROW_COST_KNEE = 64
+SATURATED_ROW_COST_SCALE = 1.0
+MMA_TILE_STEP_ROWS = 0.25
+SINGLE_REQ_TILE_STEP_ROWS = 1.5
+SECOND_WAVE_STEP_ROWS = 2.0
+
+# Context-length marginal row-cost scaling: above 8,192 tokens, each
+# verification row scans more KV/index pages in the 8 V4.1 indexer layers
+# (4 reindex layers saturating at 16,384 candidate positions, and 4 source
+# layers scaling linearly across the active context). Because indexer and
+# sparse-MLA work is per-row rather than shared across a weight tile, its
+# excess cost above 1.0x is added uncoalesced per verification row.
+CONTEXT_ROW_COST_KNEE = 8192
+CONTEXT_REINDEX_SATURATION = 16384
+CONTEXT_REINDEX_WEIGHT = 0.12
+CONTEXT_SOURCE_SPAN = 65536
+CONTEXT_SOURCE_SLOPE = 0.22
+CONTEXT_MAX_ROW_COST_SCALE = 2.25
 
 
